        "titulo": "Review: forms and uses of the imperfetto",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: forms: «-vo, -vi, -va, -vamo, -vate, -vano» after the infinitive without «-re». STEP 2: old stems: «bevevo, dicevo, facevo». STEP 3: «essere»: «ero, eri, era, eravamo, eravate, erano». STEP 4: uses: habits, ongoing actions, age, time, weather, states and descriptions. STEP 5: «avevo dieci anni», «faceva freddo» and «erano le otto» are the three verbs behind English «was».",
        "comparacao": "The imperfetto covers «used to», «would» (habit) and «was -ing». English needs three different structures, Italian uses one. The mistakes are in the choice of verb for age, weather and time, not in the form of the tense.",
